            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Russian for a graduation party, then the Russian for a generation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: помолвка",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "помолвка (pomólvka) — \"an engagement\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "После помолвки они поехали к родителям. Pósle pomólvki oní poyékhali k rodítelyam. After the engagement they went to visit the parents."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "помолвка (pomólvka) is built on помолвить \"to promise in marriage\", from молвить \"to say\", inherited from Proto-Slavic mŭlviti (EtymDB): a spoken promise."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
